# API routes, services and Prisma

The backend is Next.js Route Handlers (`app/api/**/route.ts`) calling named-function
services (`server/services/*`) that use the Prisma singleton (`lib/prisma.ts`). There is no
ORM layer beyond Prisma, no zod, no external API server. Copy the shape of
`app/api/bonus/route.ts` + `server/services/bonusService.ts` for new domains.

## Route Handler shape

```ts
export const dynamic = "force-dynamic"; // routes that read cookies or user data

export async function PATCH(request: Request) {
  try {
    const body: ViewedBonusBody = await request.json();
    const userData = await cookieService.getUserDataFromCookies(); // throws 401 response
    const bonus = await bonusService.markViewedBonus(
      +body.bonusId,
      userData.id
    );
    return NextResponse.json(bonus);
  } catch (error) {
    return apiCatchErrorHandler({
      error,
      message: "Ошибка при отметке бонуса",
    });
  }
}
```

- One exported function per HTTP method. Dynamic segments: `type Params = Promise<{ id: string }>`
  and `const { id } = await segmentData.params;` (Next 15).
- Query params: `new URL(request.url).searchParams.get("...")`; coerce with `+value` or
  `Number(value)` and validate before use.
- **Error protocol:** `ApiError.badRequest / unauthorized / forbidden / internal` return a
  `NextResponse` with `{ success: false, message, error? }`. Services `throw` them; handlers
  end with `return apiCatchErrorHandler({ error, message })` (`utils/errorHandler.ts`), which
  returns a thrown `NextResponse` as-is and wraps anything else as a 400. Use this helper in
  every handler instead of hand-written `instanceof NextResponse` branches.
- Messages are Russian and user-facing (the client shows `error.data.message`). Never put
  stack traces, SQL, tokens or emails in `message`.
- Response shape is the domain object (`NextResponse.json(bonus)`), typed on the client in
  `models/*` or from `@prisma/client`. Keep the RTK endpoint and the handler in sync.

## Authentication and authorization

- Auth is a `refreshToken` httpOnly cookie (`REFRESH_TOKEN_COOKIE`) holding a `jose` HS256 JWT;
  the `UserDto` is serialized into the `iss` claim. Read it only through
  `cookieService.getUserDataFromCookies()` (throws `ApiError.unauthorized()`) or
  `tokenService.validateRefreshToken()`. Never parse the cookie elsewhere.
- Cookies are set with `httpOnly: true, sameSite: "none", secure: true` via
  `cookieService.setTokensToCookies`.
- `middleware.ts` only guards `GET /api/users/:id`. **Every other protected handler must check
  auth itself** - any route returning or mutating a user's data calls
  `getUserDataFromCookies()` first.
- Admin-only actions check `userData.role === "ADMIN"` server-side and return
  `ApiError.forbidden(...)` otherwise. Client gating (`useAdminRoute`) is UX only, not security.
- Public GETs (consultations, feature flags, banking) stay unauthenticated on purpose.
  Admin-only handlers follow `GET` in `app/api/users/route.ts`: call
  `getUserDataFromCookies()` first, then throw `ApiError.forbidden(...)` with the message
  «Доступ только для администратора.» when `userData.role !== "ADMIN"`. Keep every inline
  code span on one line in these rules - the editor's Prettier wraps `.mdc` differently
  from the CLI when a span breaks across lines.

## Validation at the boundary

- Body types are TS assertions (`const body: PurchaseBody = await request.json()`), so
  validate what matters by hand before touching Prisma: required fields present, numbers
  coerced, enums checked against the Prisma enum, emails normalized (`trim().toLowerCase()`).
  Throw `ApiError.badRequest("...")` with a Russian message.
- Regexes and limits shared with the client live in `app/constants/validation.ts`.

## Services and DTOs

- Services are **named async functions** in `server/services/<domain>Service.ts`, imported as
  `import * as bonusService from "@/server/services/bonusService"`. No classes.
- Service shape: `try { ...prisma...; if (conflict) throw ApiError.badRequest(...); return result; }
catch (error) { throw catchErrorHandler({ error, message: "Ошибка ..." }); }`.
- DTOs (`server/dtos/*`) are factory functions (`getUserDto({...})`) that return exactly the
  fields the client may see. **Never return `password`, token rows, reset links or raw
  Prisma user records** from a handler - map through a DTO.
- Email goes through `server/services/mailService.ts` with templates in
  `server/helpers/email/`; never log recipients or links.

## Prisma usage

- Import the client only from `@/lib/prisma` (the singleton). Never `new PrismaClient()`.
- The main user model is `Users` (accessor `prisma.users`). The lowercase `model users` in the
  schema is a leftover from the Vercel example - do not use it or extend it.
- Prefer `select`/`include` that match what the DTO needs; `orderBy: { createdAt: "desc" }`
  for lists.
- Multi-write flows (registration + wallet + bonus, purchase + bonus) must use
  `prisma.$transaction([...])` or the interactive form so a failure cannot leave half the
  rows. Existing `Promise.all` chains are debt; fix them when you touch that flow.
- Environment-dependent filters use `getEnvironment()` (`server/helpers/envKeys.ts`), e.g.
  consultations are `PUBLISHED` only in production.
- Catch Prisma errors in the service and translate to a Russian `ApiError` message; never
  leak `PrismaClientKnownRequestError` text to the client.

## Schema conventions (`prisma/schema.prisma`)

- Models PascalCase singular where possible (new models); fields camelCase; relation
  fields named after the model; `id Int @id @default(autoincrement())`; `createdAt DateTime
@default(now())`; `updatedAt DateTime?` set by the service (`@updatedAt` is fine on new
  models).
- Enums UPPER_SNAKE_CASE values; display mapping (currency symbols) lives in
  `prisma/enumAdapter.ts`, never in the schema `@map` for new enums.
- Run `npx prisma format` after editing; keep the datasource `url`/`directUrl` env names.
- When a model changes, update in the same change: `models/*` types, DTOs, services, the RTK
  endpoint types, and `prisma/seed.ts` if seeded.

## Database safety

- The project uses `prisma db push` (no migrations folder) and `npm run build` runs
  `prisma db push && prisma db seed` on Vercel. **Before any schema change:** confirm which
  database `POSTGRES_PRISMA_URL` points at, run `npm run db-backup`, then follow the
  `prisma-schema-change` skill.
- Never run `prisma db push --force-reset`, `--accept-data-loss`, `prisma migrate reset`,
  `DROP`/`TRUNCATE`, or delete rows in bulk without the developer's explicit go-ahead in the
  same conversation and a fresh backup.
- `prisma/seed.ts` only inserts consultations whose `title` is not yet present
  (`findMany` followed by `createMany` inside `$transaction`); it never updates existing
  rows. Its `main()` call is currently commented out - known state, do not "fix" it
  silently.

## Secrets and logging

- Read secrets only via `server/helpers/envKeys.ts` / `helpers/token.ts`; never inline a
  value, never read secrets in client code (only `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` reaches the browser).
- Privileged accounts come from env: admin emails via `ADMIN_EMAILS` and `isAdminEmail()`
  in `server/helpers/envKeys.ts`. Never hardcode emails and never add a master password or
  any other login bypass.
- No `console.log` of request bodies, tokens, cookies, emails or passwords. If you need
  server diagnostics, log a short Russian or English message without personal data.
